Loom-State

Creative Catalyst: The sound was reverse-engineered from a corrupted cassette found in a time capsule, preserving the ghost-notes of an impossible party.

Loom-State is the sound of an orchestra being pulled through a voltage-starved acid box. It discards the hedonistic abandon of traditional house for a rigid, textile-like precision. Imagine the "squelch" of a TB-303 acting as a metronomic loom, weaving aggressive, high-drama string swells into tight, claustrophobic arrangements. It is orchestral, but stripped of its grandeur, left only with the rhythmic friction of a machine trying to emulate a symphonic swell.

Genre DNA
*   Tempo & Pulse: 114–122 BPM; a jagged, non-swinging grid that mimics the mechanical clatter of a high-speed industrial loom.
*   Harmonic Palette: Phrygian-dominant scales that refuse to resolve, favoring tense, semi-tonal collisions between brass and acid-synths.
*   Production Signatures: 
    *   "Tape-Grafting": Physically splicing high-frequency orchestral string attacks onto the decay tail of acid bass stabs.
    *   "Resonant Threading": Applying extreme band-pass filters to entire string sections to make them sound like they are emerging from a narrow pipe.
    *   "Glitch-Conducting": Using corrupted time-code data from the original cassette as a secondary percussion layer.
*   Dynamics: A "Staccato-Swell" structure where the track creates an illusion of orchestral blooming, only to have the sound abruptly "cut" by a sharp acid-filter reset.

Scene & Origin Lore
The movement began in the abandoned textile mills of Lodz, where scavengers discovered a data-rich magnetic ribbon inside a lead-lined time capsule. They wear "Weft-Armor"—garments made of conductive copper thread and velvet that stiffen when exposed to high-decibel resonant frequencies. Their rituals involve "Unspooling," a 48-hour event where the music never loops, but constantly evolves based on the magnetic interference of the audience’s own metallic jewelry. They don’t dance; they walk in perfectly synchronized, intricate patterns, miming the motion of a spinning jenny.

Instruments: Modified Roland TB-303 (Acid), granular-synthesized cello (Orchestral), Mellotron tape-loops (Atmospheric), and digital impulse-response arrays (Trance-like).

For Fans Of: Autechre, William Basinski, Arca, and mid-period Gas.

